Yes. This changes the architecture in an important way. Do not make the file-processing service and the BCBS messaging/response-processing service a single failover unit. Treat them as two independently scalable planes:

1. File Processing Plane — DC-local
2. Payment/Messaging Processing Plane — Active-Active across both DCs

That allows DC2 to continue processing its own files when DC1 storage is unavailable, while all healthy containers in both DCs continue consuming and producing BCBS messages.

