The file is a transport mechanism only. Once its business data is durably accepted, processing should become event-driven and independent of the source storage.

The key architectural rule

Storage failure should stop only file intake for that DC—not payment processing, Outbox publishing, BCBS consumption/production, settlement processing, or other already-ingested business workflows.

This separation gives you much better resilience than traditional DC-level active/passive failover and is particularly appropriate for your ACH pre-fund → earmark → acknowledgement → settlement workflow.

