Yes—support both resilient S3 and DC-specific storage. Make storage a pluggable infrastructure capability, keep DB-backed processing ownership independent of storage, and make batch/payment/messaging processing active-active across both DCs.

That gives you a very strong failure model: loss of DC1 storage stops only DC1’s ability to discover/read new physical files; it does not stop already-ingested payment processing, BCBS messaging, settlement, or DC2 file intake.
