Storage determines where the physical file is read from; it must not determine which DC is allowed to process the resulting payment events.

So your final requirement should state:

The ACH application shall support S3 and NFS as interchangeable file-storage providers. The storage provider shall be configurable without changing business-processing logic. File ownership, batch ownership, payment processing, Outbox publishing, BCBS messaging, reservation processing, settlement processing, and reconciliation shall remain independent of the underlying file-storage technology.

That gives you the flexibility to deploy with NFS initially and move to S3 later without redesigning the core ACH processing architecture.


